00:27:59.970 --> 00:28:02.570
times the length of v.

00:28:02.570 --> 00:28:04.110
What do we have on the left?

00:28:04.110 --> 00:28:07.370
I have the absolute value of the
dot product of u and v.

00:28:07.370 --> 00:28:08.910
What is that?

00:28:08.910 --> 00:28:09.910
Yeah.

00:28:12.370 --> 00:28:15.750
I would have a squared plus b
squared,

00:28:15.750 --> 00:28:16.750
right?

00:28:19.150 --> 00:28:22.250
If what I did was have ab and
ab,

00:28:22.250 --> 00:28:22.970
right?

00:28:22.970 --> 00:28:25.050
I would give a times a plus b
times b.

00:28:25.050 --> 00:28:27.490
That would be what I would have
on the left.

00:28:27.490 --> 00:28:29.150
And on the right, what would I
have?

00:28:29.150 --> 00:28:31.610
What's the length of u?

00:28:31.610 --> 00:28:34.110
It's the square root of the sum
of the squares of its

00:28:34.110 --> 00:28:35.110
components.

00:28:35.110 --> 00:28:37.910
And what are those components?

00:28:37.910 --> 00:28:40.690
a and b, so it should be the
square root of a squared plus b

00:28:40.690 --> 00:28:41.690
squared.

00:28:41.730 --> 00:28:45.090
But since here, in this
hypothetical example, I made v

00:28:45.090 --> 00:28:46.870
be the same vector,

00:28:46.870 --> 00:28:49.750
its length would also be the
same thing.

00:28:49.750 --> 00:28:52.630
So I could just square this
whole thing.

00:28:52.630 --> 00:28:54.770
But then when you realize that I
told you that a and b had to be

00:28:54.770 --> 00:28:55.770
non-negative,

00:28:56.230 --> 00:28:59.230
even if they weren't
non-negative,

00:28:59.810 --> 00:29:02.270
this can't be negative, a
squared plus b squared.

00:29:02.270 --> 00:29:03.810
So then when the absolute values
drop,

00:29:03.810 --> 00:29:06.030
all this tells you is that a
squared plus b squared is less

00:29:06.030 --> 00:29:08.450
than or equal to a squared plus
b squared.

00:29:08.450 --> 00:29:09.950
Which is not super insightful.

00:29:09.950 --> 00:29:12.310
We knew that already.

00:29:12.310 --> 00:29:15.310
So that's a first hint when
dealing with these

00:29:15.310 --> 00:29:16.810
Cauchy-Schwarz inequality
questions.

00:29:17.530 --> 00:29:20.250
It's almost never the case that
the u and v are supposed to be

00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:21.050
the same.

00:29:21.050 --> 00:29:24.970
You're supposed to arrange them
in a way that when you take the

00:29:24.970 --> 00:29:26.810
dot product of the two, that
gives you something different

00:29:26.810 --> 00:29:29.810
than just multiplying the
lengths independently.

00:29:30.310 --> 00:29:32.250
So what's the next thing you
might try? Well,

00:29:32.250 --> 00:29:32.910
as was hinted,

00:29:32.910 --> 00:29:37.410
maybe we try v being ba.

00:29:37.590 --> 00:29:39.650
What does that give us?

00:29:39.650 --> 00:29:41.690
Now on the left-hand side,

00:29:41.690 --> 00:29:43.950
what do I get?

00:29:43.950 --> 00:29:48.310
I have the absolute value of
what?

00:29:48.310 --> 00:29:54.990
If u is ab and v is ba, what do
I have on the left-hand side?

00:29:54.990 --> 00:29:57.770
2 times ab, good.

00:29:57.770 --> 00:30:00.030
And I can drop the absolute
value, Because again, I know

00:30:00.030 --> 00:30:01.350
here,

00:30:01.790 --> 00:30:05.330
I told you that both A and B are
not negative.

00:30:05.330 --> 00:30:08.390
And on the right, what do I
have?

00:30:08.390 --> 00:30:08.710
Well,

00:30:08.710 --> 00:30:09.930
u is the same as before.

00:30:09.930 --> 00:30:14.510
Its length is the square root of
a squared plus b squared.

00:30:14.510 --> 00:30:17.310
And here, all I did was shuffle
the elements in v

00:30:17.310 --> 00:30:19.250
so it doesn't change its length.

00:30:19.250 --> 00:30:19.950
So really,

00:30:19.950 --> 00:30:22.170
that is still being squared.

00:30:22.170 --> 00:30:24.010
So this almost looks like what I
want.

00:30:24.010 --> 00:30:26.310
If I write this again,

00:30:26.310 --> 00:30:31.750
I have 2ab is less than or equal
to a squared plus b squared,

00:30:31.750 --> 00:30:36.230
which means ab is less than or
equal to a squared plus b

00:30:36.230 --> 00:30:38.330
squared over 2.

00:30:38.330 --> 00:30:42.770
This is like similar-ish to the
thing I told you to prove.

00:30:42.770 --> 00:30:46.890
But everything in the thing I
told you to prove is a square

00:30:46.890 --> 00:30:49.390
root of these variables, right?
On the left,

00:30:49.390 --> 00:30:51.030
we have an ab here,

00:30:51.030 --> 00:30:53.370
but we wanted a square root of
ab.

00:30:53.370 --> 00:30:54.570
And on the right,

00:30:54.570 --> 00:30:57.330
we have an a squared plus b
squared on the numerator, but

00:30:57.330 --> 00:30:59.410
you wanted just an a plus b.

00:30:59.410 --> 00:31:01.130
So what's the solution?

00:31:01.130 --> 00:31:03.750
Just square root everything in
the vector that we define.

00:31:03.750 --> 00:31:05.890
We defined u and v.
We can do that however we'd

00:31:05.890 --> 00:31:06.890
like.

00:31:06.890 --> 00:31:11.450
So if we define u and v to be

00:31:11.450 --> 00:31:15.990
root a root b

00:31:15.990 --> 00:31:21.990
and v to be root b root a,

00:31:22.090 --> 00:31:24.650
then the Cauchy-Schwarz
inequality tells us well the

00:31:24.650 --> 00:31:28.590
absolute value of their dot
product is less than or equal to

00:31:28.590 --> 00:31:31.690
the product of their lengths.

00:31:31.690 --> 00:31:33.510
What do we have on the left?

00:31:33.510 --> 00:31:35.070
I have the absolute value of
what?

00:31:35.070 --> 00:31:39.570
Guess you want to remind me.

00:31:41.190 --> 00:31:42.190
Good,

00:31:45.190 --> 00:31:47.830
because I have square root of a
times square root of b plus

00:31:47.830 --> 00:31:49.470
square root of b times the
square root of a.

00:31:49.470 --> 00:31:53.110
That just looks like 2 times the
square root of AB.

00:31:53.110 --> 00:31:55.750
Again, that can't be negative,
so I'll drop the absolute value.

00:31:55.750 --> 00:31:58.250
On the left, what do I have?

00:31:58.250 --> 00:32:00.030
Well, what's the length of u?

00:32:00.030 --> 00:32:06.030
It's the square root of the
square root of A squared

00:32:06.470 --> 00:32:10.430
plus the square root of B
squared.

00:32:10.430 --> 00:32:13.630
And then the length of V is also
the same thing.

00:32:13.630 --> 00:32:15.950
So if we really want to write
this out thoroughly,

00:32:15.950 --> 00:32:18.950
say something like this.

00:32:22.970 --> 00:32:24.070
On the left,

00:32:24.070 --> 00:32:25.150
I still have my square,

00:32:25.150 --> 00:32:27.210
2 times the square root of AB,
and on the right, what do I

00:32:27.210 --> 00:32:27.690
have?

00:32:27.690 --> 00:32:30.010
Well, these two things are the
same, so I can keep one of them

00:32:30.010 --> 00:32:31.570
and drop the square root.

00:32:31.570 --> 00:32:33.710
And then, what's the square root
of A?

00:32:33.710 --> 00:32:34.570
Squared?

00:32:34.570 --> 00:32:35.590
Well, that's just A.

00:32:35.590 --> 00:32:36.850
And what's the square root of B?

00:32:36.850 --> 00:32:38.170
Squared, that's just B.

00:32:38.170 --> 00:32:39.390
So on the left,

00:32:39.390 --> 00:32:43.290
I have the square root of A plus
B squared,

00:32:43.290 --> 00:32:46.930
so this tells me 2 times the
square root of AB is just less

00:32:46.930 --> 00:32:50.150
than or equal to A plus B, which
is exactly the thing I told you

00:32:50.150 --> 00:32:50.830
to prove,

00:32:50.830 --> 00:32:54.510
if you divide both sides by 2.

00:32:54.510 --> 00:32:56.430
So I think this is kind of
interesting.

00:32:56.430 --> 00:32:58.590
This inequality has nothing to
do with vectors, yet we were

00:32:58.590 --> 00:33:02.830
able to use just properties of
the dot product and an

00:33:02.830 --> 00:33:05.730
inequality we defined with that
to prove seemingly unrelated

00:33:05.730 --> 00:33:06.730
things.

00:33:07.590 --> 00:33:09.990
So this Cauchy-Schwarz
inequality comes up a lot.

00:33:11.210 --> 00:33:12.510
And like I said,

00:33:12.510 --> 00:33:15.210
a common midterm one question in
the past,

00:33:15.210 --> 00:33:17.070
I don't know if it'll the future
midterm one question, haven't

00:33:17.070 --> 00:33:18.730
wrote it yet,

00:33:18.730 --> 00:33:23.370
has been use the Cauchy-Schwarz
inequality to prove some other

00:33:23.370 --> 00:33:27.120
fact about numbers provided in
the question.

00:33:28.930 --> 00:33:31.930
Questions with questions like
this.

00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:38.310
And I guess one thing I'll say
here is that there's no way I

00:33:38.310 --> 00:33:40.690
was really expecting you to be
able to know that this is how

00:33:40.690 --> 00:33:42.470
you were supposed to use the
Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to

00:33:42.470 --> 00:33:43.870
arrive here.
There's no way you would know

00:33:43.870 --> 00:33:46.430
how to do this before this.

00:33:46.430 --> 00:33:48.890
As you practice more and more of
these, now that you have this

00:33:48.890 --> 00:33:50.850
example in your toolkit,

00:33:50.850 --> 00:33:54.790
you are way better equipped to
see a new question that asks

00:33:54.790 --> 00:33:57.040
something like this.

00:33:57.710 --> 00:34:01.010
And you're better equipped to be
able to make informed guesses as

00:34:01.010 --> 00:34:02.750
to what to put in u and v.

00:34:02.750 --> 00:34:04.850
And what I hopefully tried to
illustrate is that you're not

00:34:04.850 --> 00:34:07.270
supposed to just look at it and
know what u and v are supposed

00:34:07.270 --> 00:34:07.930
to be.

00:34:07.930 --> 00:34:10.150
You try some things, it doesn't
work, and then you use that to

00:34:10.150 --> 00:34:14.650
update your guess and use that
to arrive at a solution.

00:34:14.990 --> 00:34:17.850
Can we get partial credit for
identifying that we would have

00:34:17.850 --> 00:34:20.030
to use Cauchy-Schwartz here?

00:34:20.030 --> 00:34:22.550
Usually in a question like this,
we will say, so use the

00:34:22.550 --> 00:34:25.250
Cauchy-Schwartz inequality to do
that.

00:34:25.250 --> 00:34:26.170
Yeah,

00:34:26.170 --> 00:34:27.670
good question.

00:34:28.090 --> 00:34:31.090
Other questions with that?

00:34:32.190 --> 00:34:34.070
But I guess what I'll say to
that is,

00:34:34.070 --> 00:34:36.910
there are only so many patterns
that this can follow.

